{title: Take My Life and Let It Be}
{artist: Frances Havergal}
{key: F}
{time: 3/4}
{tempo: 84}

Verse 1
[F]Take my life and [C]let it [F]be [Bb]consecrated, [C]Lord, to [F]thee;
take my moments [C]and my [F]days, [Bb]let them flow in [C]ceaseless [F]praise.

Verse 2
[F]Take my hands, and [C]let them move [F]at [Bb]the [C]impulse of [F]Thy
love. Take my [C]feet, and [F]let [Bb]them be swift and beautiful [C]for [F]Thee.

Verse 3
[F]Take my voice, and [C]let me [F]sing [Bb]always, [C]only, for [F]my
King. Take my [C]lips, and [F]let [Bb]them be filled with messages [C]from [F]Thee.

Verse 4
[F]Take my silver and [C]my gold; [F]not [Bb]a [C]mite would [F]I
withhold. Take my [C]intellect, and [F]use [Bb]every pow'r as Thou [C]shalt [F]choose.

Verse 5
[F]Take my will, and [C]make it Thine; [F]it [Bb]shall [C]be no [F]longer
mine. Take my heart, [C]it is [F]Thine [Bb]own; it shall be Thy [C]royal [F]throne.
